{
  "id": "reflex-integration",
  "term": "reflex integration",
  "definition": "Reflex integration refers to the developmental process or therapeutic focus of helping primitive early-life reflexes become inhibited as the central nervous system matures, so more controlled posture and purposeful movement can emerge. In this context, it is linked to methods such as Vojta and Dynamic Neuromuscular Stabilization that aim to facilitate neuromuscular and postural control.",
